   "evidence": "No such lemma exists: `grep -rn \"formClass Q hQ = x\\|Surjective.*formClass\\|exists_formClass\" code/TauCeti` returns no matches, and `RegularFormClass/Basic.lean:531-573` stops at `exists_presentedForm_equivalent`/`formClass_presentedForm`/`rank_formClass`; `LocalField/QuadraticForm/Realization.lean:113` is purely class-level. The PR itself follows the opposite (correct) pattern at the real place, extracting `QuadraticForm.exists_nondegenerate_and_sigPos_eq_and_sigNeg_eq` into `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/QuadraticForm/Real.lean:242` rather than inlining it.",
   "file": "TauCeti/NumberTheory/QuadraticForm/Global/LocalRealization.lean",
   "fix": "Add to `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/QuadraticForm/RegularFormClass/Basic.lean` (next to `formClass_presentedForm`) the general lemma `theorem exists_quadraticForm_formClass_eq {n : \u2115} (x : RegularFormClass K) (hx : x.rank = n) : \u2203 (Q : QuadraticForm K (Fin n \u2192 K)) (hQ : Q.Nondegenerate), formClass Q hQ = x`, and derive `exists_quadraticForm_atFinitePlace` from it by rewriting `hxd`/`hxs`.",
   "issue": "The proof of `exists_quadraticForm_atFinitePlace` (lines 213\u2013222: `Quotient.inductionOn`, `RegularFormClass.rank_mk`, `presentedForm`, `nondegenerate_presentedForm`, `formClass_presentedForm`) uses nothing about `K_v` or `I`; it is the general statement that every `x : RegularFormClass F` of rank `n` is `formClass` of a form on `Fin n \u2192 F`, proved only in this special case. Any other consumer of `RegularFormClass.exists_of_realization` (e.g. \u00a77.2, or a complex/real-place analogue) must redo the induction.",
   "line": "207"
  }
 ],
